<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Pydna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/168-bce">168 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-macedonian-war">Third Macedonian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Pydna was fought on 22 June 168 BCE near Pydna in Macedonia, where a Roman army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Lucius Aemilius Paullus</a> defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus of Macedon</a>. Broken up on rough ground, the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> was cut to pieces by the more flexible Roman legions. The battle ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-macedonian-war">Third Macedonian War</a> and the Antigonid monarchy, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-roman-province">Macedonia</a> into four republics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-pydna.jpg" alt="Battle of Pydna" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marsyas (original map); Mkr bu50 (English translation) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_battle_of_Pydna-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
